#: library/processes/multi-locale-translation.bpmn:20
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Translate one or more layers into several locales at once, as a team: one source-language lead, one translator per locale, an untainted round trip, and the owner's merge window. The result is unofficial, on main, and kept current by a watcher. You are in this process when more than one locale is being produced from the same source at the same time. `translation-workflow` is the machine half for one catalogue and `human-translation-workflow` is the path to an official, signed-off translation; this process is the team around them. It extracts ONCE: every locale starts from the same templates, merged to main in one source PR before any locale begins, and no translator re-extracts. Each locale then lands as its own PR to main, never into the source branch, and a source PR's branch receives nothing after it merges. Two things are never done in a translation: fixing the source (a source-text error is reported as one issue to the lead), and editing a FHIR resource inline (terms go into one CodeSystem supplement per locale). Officiality is not decided here: every catalogue is written unofficial, and a person makes it official through human-translation-workflow."
msgstr ""

